      "content": "…; collection Paul Joseph Constantin Gabriël (1828-1903), Haarlem, Amsterdam, Brussel and Scheveningen, before 1888;{De Bruyn Kops 1969, p. 37.} his sale, Amsterdam (F. Muller), 14 June 1927 <em>sqq.</em>, no. 292; …; the dealer Unger en Van Mens, Rotterdam {HNA, SNK archive, 2.08.42, inv. no. 756, no 3689}…; collection Gijsbertus Anthonius van Rede, Bennekom, before 1945;{HNA, SNK archive, inv.no. 164, letter 17 June 1950.} from whom stolen during WWII, ca. 1940-45;{HNA, SNK archive, inv. no. 756, no 3689.} …; anonymous sale, Amsterdam (P. Brandt), 5 November 1968 <em>sqq.</em>, no. 313, fl. 307.85, to the museum",
